# registries.yaml — the NODE-side half of the ghcr pull-through cache
# (./registry-mirror.yaml). Installed to /etc/rancher/k3s/registries.yaml by
# ./install-registry-mirror.sh, which is the only thing that expands the one
# placeholder below. Item `livespec-h96p`.
#
# A TEMPLATE AND NOT A FILE, for exactly one reason: the endpoint differs by
# node role, and there is no spelling that is right on both. The cache's store
# is a hostPath on the node carrying the `ci-cache` tier, so the SERVER reaches
# it on loopback and an AGENT must reach it at that node's LAN address. The
# installer derives which from the run's profile — `CLUSTER_ROLE` for the role,
# `CLUSTER_JOIN_ADDRESS` for the carrier's address on an agent — so the value
# comes from the same committed profile every other node fact comes from
# rather than being typed at a call site.
#
# k3s reads this file at START, so installing it changes nothing until the next
# k3s start. That restart is NOT this installer's to take: it kills every
# running job on the pool (../../k3s-config/config.yaml says the same about its
# own `tls-san` list). Install it, and let the next reboot or maintenance
# window pick it up.
#
# WHY ONLY ghcr.io IS LISTED. A pull-through instance proxies exactly one
# upstream, and this one proxies ghcr. Every other registry the node pulls from
# — docker.io for the mirror's own image, registry.k8s.io, quay.io — is absent
# here on purpose and keeps behaving exactly as it does today. A registry NOT
# named in this file is never affected by it.
#
# WHAT HAPPENS WHEN THE MIRROR IS DOWN: nothing that matters. Containerd has an
# implicit default endpoint that k3s documents as "always tried as a last
# resort, even if there are other endpoints listed for that registry in
# registries.yaml", so a refused connection to the mirror costs one failed dial
# and the pull then goes to ghcr as before. That fallback is what makes this
# file safe to install ahead of the mirror ever running, and it is why
# `--disable-default-registry-endpoint` — the k3s node flag that removes it —
# must never be set on this pool.
mirrors:
  ghcr.io:
    endpoint:
      - "@MIRROR_ENDPOINT@"
